tail)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Traumatic Acute Subdural Hematoma with Bridging Vein Rupture", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.10027280100272801, "posterior": 0.12812541216814574, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The absence of cranial nerve deficits or cerebellar signs directly contradicts B3 (posterior circulation injury), making this option unlikely to explain the current presentation."], "evidence_against": ["High-velocity trauma can cause bridging vein tearing for acute subdural hematoma, but the patient's rapid post-traumatic decline contradicts a subacute pattern. This weakly disfavors B2 while preserving support for more immediate hemorrhagic mechanisms."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of prior intracranial bleeds or coagulopathy?", "Is the bleeding location temporal/parietofrontal?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Head CT for 'crescent sign' confirmation", "Coagulation panel"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 1.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Cerebellar/Brainstem Traumatic Hemorrhage", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.04946017749137978, "danger": 0.95, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of cranial nerve deficits or cerebellar signs directly contradicts B3 (posterior circulation injury), making this option unlikely to explain the current presentation."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Skull Base Fracture with Cerebrospinal Fluid Leak and Hemorrhage", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06594690332183972, "danger